<title>ITALY: Italy's Ina sells stake in SIAC to EULER.</title>
<headline>Italy's Ina sells stake in SIAC to EULER.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian insurer Ina said it was selling a 9.25 percent stake in Societa Italiana Assicurazioni Crediti (SIAC) to France's EULER with an option for EULER to buy a further 45 percent within the year.</p>
<p>The Ina/Assitalia group holds a 62 percent stake in SIAC.</p>
<p>The main shareholder of EULER, previously Compagnie Financiere SFAC, is Assurances Generales de France.</p>
